  {
   "key": "0x60..0x6F",
   "name": "start break",
   "regions": [
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:MC68681.raw.txt",
     "lines": "1743-1749"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/mc68681.cpp",
     "function": "duart_channel::write_CR",
     "case": [
      "6"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "CRA[6:4] = 110 is the Start Break command.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:MC68681.raw.txt",
       "lines": "1743",
       "sha": "7fe2ac93e420c48366c21bb6cb7b1bfe9d8053559f9bf24510a391f6da6d1d9f"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Start break forces TxDA low when the character being transmitted completes, and the transmitter must be enabled for it to be accepted.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:MC68681.raw.txt",
       "lines": "1743-1749",
       "sha": "6e46dd35cdba297623fbecc218f9cf638f709738a706eb4ebaaee7b79991eda4"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "101",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "differs",
     "text": "MAME sets m_tx_break without checking that the transmitter is enabled, leaves the TxD output to a TODO, and in loopback sets the break bit and queues a break.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/mc68681.cpp",
       "lines": "1765-1776",
       "sha": "f7c59726ea057e63e49c533c3b64ef4c2b56eb156216e5c85845fb04b53853e9"
      },
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/mc68681.cpp",
       "lines": "1777-1780",
       "sha": "412a5390d4e08f2bc855a38dbe26dfa7a68b77108bc0876ec428a51f0ed154c9"
      }
     ],
     "row": "2"
    }
   ],
   "closed": [
