  {
   "key": "0xC0..0xFF",
   "name": "xr68c681 power",
   "regions": [
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:XR68C681.raw.txt",
     "lines": "705-715"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/mc68681.cpp",
     "function": "xr68c681_device::write",
     "case": [
      "0x0c"
     ]
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/mc68681.cpp",
     "function": "xr68c681_device::write",
     "case": [
      "0x0d"
     ]
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/mc68681.cpp",
     "function": "xr68c681_device::write",
     "case": [
      "0x0e"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "variant": "XR68C681",
     "text": "The four codes of this range are Set Standby Mode, Set Active Mode, and two reserved codes; both standby commands act through channel A.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:XR68C681.raw.txt",
       "lines": "705-715",
       "sha": "c5b28f02be60874c9d5c10c7b03c24f7d739516bcdf12fb446b2be9cb293fdf9"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "variant": "XR68C681",
     "text": "Set standby mode removes power from the transmitters, receivers, counter/timer and other circuits, placing the whole DUART in low power mode.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:XR68C681.raw.txt",
       "lines": "705-710",
       "sha": "f3b1b20945fb6787c0c5ce0611b05937325fbcd247793a97bc8dbc22663a02b8"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "variant": "XR68C681",
     "text": "Set active mode leaves the standby mode and resumes normal operation.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:XR68C681.raw.txt",
       "lines": "711-713",
       "sha": "c73d841eee17f0a25821b2c49af7ded6aac4e464a9fa75898ccb9cf2265886e5"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "4",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "variant": "XR68C681",
     "text": "Normal operation is also restored by a hardware reset.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:XR68C681.raw.txt",
       "lines": "709-710",
       "sha": "0a223892c6c1fd03808cdbb7adc1271c22b2f800dcfa817aa9135ffbf8b14a55"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "5",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "variant": "XR68C681",
     "text": "The last two entries of the table are reserved codes.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:XR68C681.raw.txt",
       "lines": "714-715",
       "sha": "a648c8d21fab58ed5d86e61c76609253b58391f89f0b6ad9b41858c09a5343b1"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "101",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "absent",
     "text": "MAME's case for these codes only masks the byte to its low nibble, with a TODO for the low power mode; nothing places the chip in standby.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/mc68681.cpp",
       "lines": "901-906",
       "sha": "77cb3bf4ed4a5625e6adf26f3da757b1ebd01f795f53ec79a9cb31895a2563f7"
      }
     ],
     "row": "2"
    },
    {
     "n": "102",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "absent",
     "text": "MAME's case for these codes only masks the byte to its low nibble; nothing returns the chip from standby.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/mc68681.cpp",
       "lines": "901-906",
       "sha": "77cb3bf4ed4a5625e6adf26f3da757b1ebd01f795f53ec79a9cb31895a2563f7"
